<title>SINGAPORE: South Korea's KEPCO awards LSWR to Ssangyong Corp.</title>
<headline>South Korea's KEPCO awards LSWR to Ssangyong Corp.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Electric Power Corp (KEPCO) said on Monday it has awarded its tender to buy November low sulphur waxy residue (LSWR) to Ssangyong Corp.</p>
<p>Ssangyong Corp sold the 400,000 barrels of LSWR at $1.91 per barrel over Singapore spot quotes for November 5-9 delivery, on a cost-and-freight (c-and-f) basis to Inchon.</p>
<p>In its last tender, KEPCO bought 200,000 barrels of LSWR from South Korean refiner Yukong Ltd at $2.555 per barrel over Singapore spot quotes for July 15-19 delivery c-and-f Ulsan.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65-870-3082)</p>
</text>
